build

# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` - without this, a real .env.local/.env
# present in the build context (e.g. from a local `docker build`) gets
# baked directly into an image layer, where it stays readable via `docker
# history`/`docker save` even after a later layer deletes it. Real
# deployments should inject env vars through the hosting platform instead
# of relying on a file in the image at all.
.env*